<title>AUSTRALIA: Evans Deakin wins further Westrail deal.</title>
<headline>Evans Deakin wins further Westrail deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Heavy engineering group Evans Deakin Industries Ltd said on Monday it had won a further contract for the supply of 10 new passenger railcars to Perth's Westrail.</p>
<p>The company said its share of the A$32.8 million contract was A$13.9 million.  </p>
<p>The order follows an extra six locomotives ordered by Westrail in February.</p>
<p>The new railcars are to be built at Evans Deakin's Maryborough plant in Queensland.</p>
<p>Evans Deakin shares ended unchanged at A$3.20 on turnover of 57,149 shares.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
